for name,lines,assessment in [
 ('clique_complex.rs',165,'Complete body read. Shell plus bounded simple undirected triangle census: 1..12 vertices, endpoint/loop/duplicate rejection, symmetric adjacency and i<j<k enumeration. This computes triangles and edge counts, not the full flag complex. The two graph examples are meaningful local controls; mutation accounting is only a comment.'),
 ('finite_cliques.rs',155,'Complete body read. Validates symmetric loop-free bitsets on 0..128 indexed vertices, handles the full-width mask specially, enumerates fixed-size cliques uniquely with candidate intersections, and computes maximum clique using greedy independent color classes as upper bounds. Explicit branch/output budgets refuse rather than returning partial answers. Independent exhaustive comparison on all 1100 undirected graphs with n<=5 agrees for every clique size and maximum. Empty clique and empty graph conventions are coherent. Original tests include one subset comparison and 128-vertex boundaries; no native execution.'),
 ('dowker_complex.rs',127,'Complete body read. Shell plus exact one-skeleton count from a finite relation: deduplicates columns per row and unordered column pairs globally. Isolated declared columns cannot be represented unless present in the relation; higher faces and Dowker equivalence are not constructed. Empty relation is accepted under nonempty label. No new local operation tests are present; arithmetic conversions checked, input/work count not bounded.'),
 ('vietoris_rips.rs',257,'Complete body read. Naive diameter filtration constructs vertices, edges and triangles only and returns min(max_dim,2), so requests above two lose higher simplices. Public PointCloud directly indexes distances without shape, symmetry, nonnegativity or metric validation; negative radius still includes all vertices, and negative edge distance can precede its vertices. No algorithm budget is connected to the separate generic capacity record. Two unit-segment tests cover a radius threshold only. Correct symmetric nonnegative inputs give the intended truncated flag filtration; no full metric or requested higher-dimensional guarantee.'),
 ('witness_complex.rs',233,'Complete body read. Weak-witness admission validates square symmetric nonnegative zero-diagonal distances, at most eight leading landmarks, nonempty proper member/other sets, and the max-inside<=min-outside inequality for some point. It does not require triangle inequalities, which are unnecessary for this declared dissimilarity predicate. Bit validation only checks simplex<=255 rather than the declared landmark mask; extra bits below bit eight are ignored while retained in the witness. Positive and no-witness examples omit this malformed carrier case. This local weak witness is not full witness-complex construction or all-face closure.'),
 ('filtration.rs',206,'Complete body read. Public filtration stores arbitrary simplex records. The private CertifiedFiltration checks exactly the narrow documented conditions: nonempty vertex spans, matching declared dimension, max dimension and nondecreasing values. It does not check unique ordered vertices, uniqueness, face closure or face precedence; the positive unit test explicitly admits an edge without its vertices. Counts-only certificate is not an authenticated source binding. Full persistent_homology caller performs its own stronger checks, so no bypass of that caller follows.'),
 ('filtered_complex.rs',126,'Complete body read. Label shell plus nondecreasing integer-time sequence admission with checked length/span; accepts empty times. The record contains no complexes, inclusions, differentials or persistent module, so its NotNested terminology means time order only. Local ascending and descending examples genuinely exercise that scalar predicate.'),
 ('sparse_filtration.rs',127,'Complete body read. At most 32 listed simplices, strict vertex ordering and pairwise subset/value monotonicity are checked. Missing faces are not required, empty simplices are admitted, duplicates are only constrained to equal values. Thus the every-face wording means only supplied faces, not a complete filtered simplicial complex. No sparse Rips approximation, edge collapse or error bound is implemented. Tests cover one supplied vertex/edge order and its violation.'),
 ('persistent_homology.rs',217,'Complete body read. Strong wrapper checks size, nondecreasing rational values, nonempty strictly ordered unique simplex vertices, dimensions and every codimension-one face already seen; supplied boundary must exactly equal those faces before mutation. Then F2 column reduction produces positive finite bars and essential bars using reduced-column emptiness, correctly distinguishing destroyers. Rational values are preserved and zero-length intervals discarded. Meaningful malformed-boundary test checks refusal before mutation. This wrapper repairs weaker standalone admission assumptions; public result records remain mutable and unauthenticated.'),
 ('ph_matrix_reduction.rs',210,'Complete body read. Standard sparse symmetric-difference reduction is correct on sorted unique in-range boundary supports, using the largest row as pivot and prior column elimination. Standalone public entrypoint does not enforce those preconditions and indexes pivot[low] directly; out-of-range input can panic. Full persistent_homology wrapper checks exact simplicial boundary before calling it. Only empty reduction is tested locally; generic capacity tests do not bound reduction work or validate boundary supports.'),
 ('persistence_pairing.rs',137,'Complete body read. Public pairs use None both for unpaired creators and noncreators, as the field comment acknowledges. essential_creators nevertheless returns all None entries, so it includes destroyer columns. Unchecked setter silently ignores out-of-range creators and accepts arbitrary destroyers. Separate try_admit_pair enforces new index/order/destroyer uniqueness but can overwrite an existing creator and does not enforce disjoint creator/destroyer roles or validate existing public state. Tests cover basic setter and ordered injection only; full PH result construction uses reduced-column information instead.'),
 ('persistence_diagram.rs',193,'Complete body read. Rational birth/death records and dimension filters preserve exact values but constructors accept reversed or equal endpoints; persistence returns a signed difference. No standalone admission or source binding occurs here. Generic capacity checks are unrelated to diagram validity. One finite difference test is meaningful within its narrow arithmetic scope; upstream PH constructs strictly positive finite bars.'),
 ('homology_computer.rs',193,'Complete body read. Dispatch explicitly refuses rational coefficient field instead of silently substituting F2, checks declared max dimension against request, then delegates to the stronger persistent-homology wrapper. Rational filtration values are distinct from coefficient field. Request maximum is an upper allowance, not a computation of missing higher cells. Empty and unsupported-field controls are meaningful; generic capacity record does not constrain this dispatch.')]:a.record(b+name,1,lines,assessment)
